<title>USA: PhyCor says $0.84 EPS in 1997 achievable.</title>
<headline>PhyCor says $0.84 EPS in 1997 achievable.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>PhyCor's chief financial officer on Thursday said he supported Wall Street's consensus earnings forecasts of $0.84 a share this year and $1.13 next year.</p>
<p>&quot;We think those are achievable numbers,&quot; CFO John Crawford said in an interview after speaking to Robinson-Humphrey's annual institutional conference in Atlanta.</p>
<p>The Nashville-based physicians management company earned $0.60 a share in 1996.</p>
